Revision history for PDL-IO-NYHead

0.02  2026-07-23
    - Initial standalone release, split out of the PDL-EEG project.
    - PDL::IO::NYHead: OO reader for the New York Head (sa_nyhead.mat,
      MATLAB v7.3/HDF5). Electrodes (labels + positions), leadfield
      (V_fem / V_fem_normal), head and cortex surfaces, low-resolution
      cortex reconstruction via in_from_cortex75K (PDL fancy index),
      Harvard-Oxford atlas, coordinate transforms, nearest-vertex.
    - Mesh export: to_obj / to_usda / write_mesh (thin wrappers over
      surface()/cortex()). OBJ keeps 1-based faces; USDA emits 0-based
      faceVertexIndices. examples/nyhead_export.pl with --format obj|usda.
    - PDL::IO::NYHead::H5Dump: reads MATLAB v7.3 cell-of-string fields
      (electrode / atlas names) that PDL::IO::HDF5 leaves as unresolved
      object references, via the h5dump CLI. Version-independent #refs#
      delimiter (no dependence on the h5dump object-id output format).
    - Bundled synthetic MATLAB v7.3 fixture so the test suite runs
      without the (large) real sa_nyhead.mat.
